{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q423338","formula":"C₂₇H₄₄O₇","hill":"C27H44O7","elements":["H","C","O"],"composition":{"C":27.0,"H":44.0,"O":7.0},"names":{"en":"20-hydroxyecdysone","ru":"Экдистен"},"descriptions":{"en":"20-Hydroxyecdysone (ecdysterone or 20E) is a naturally occurring ecdysteroid hormone which controls the ecdysis (moulting) and metamorphosis of arthropods. It is therefore one of the most common moulting hormones in insects, crabs, etc. Also phytoecdysteroid produced by and extracted from various plants, including Cyanotis vaga, Ajuga turkestanica and Rhaponticum carthamoides, it is thought to be a plant defense against herbivory that disrupts the reproduction of insect pests.","ru":"Экдисте́н, или Экдистерон (ecdysterone, 20 Beta-Hydroxyecdysterone, 20Е) — природное соединение стероидной структуры, выделенное из корней и корневищ левзеи сафлоровидной. Стимулирует синтез белка в организме. Обладает тонизирующим эффектом и является метаболическим средством."},"fame":11,"pubchemCid":5459840,"mass":480.6,"charge":0,"smiles":"C[C@]12CC[C@H]3C(=CC(=O)[C@H]4[C@@]3(C[C@@H]([C@@H](C4)O)O)C)[C@@]1(CC[C@@H]2[C@](C)([C@@H](CCC(C)(C)O)O)O)O","inchikey":"NKDFYOWSKOHCCO-YPVLXUMRSA-N","iupac":"(2S,3R,5R,9R,10R,13R,14S,17S)-2,3,14-trihydroxy-10,13-dimethyl-17-[(2R,3R)-2,3,6-trihydroxy-6-methylheptan-2-yl]-2,3,4,5,9,11,12,15,16,17-decahydro-1H-cyclopenta[a]phenanthren-6-one","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"pubchem","ref":"5459840","atoms":78,"license":"PubChem (NIH), public data"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":0.074,"y":0.762,"z":1.287,"el":"O"},{"x":-2.71,"y":-2.615,"z":-1.221,"el":"O"},{"x":5.457,"y":3.252,"z":-1.523,"el":"O"},{"x":-5.349,"y":-1.701,"z":-1.273,"el":"O"},{"x":4.697,"y":-2.126,"z":2.211,"el":"O"},{"x":6.862,"y":1.678,"z":0.268,"el":"O"},{"x":-8.161,"y":1.739,"z":1.177,"el":"O"},{"x":-0.43